      "id": "white-envelope",
      "term": "White Envelope",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "An envelope of legal papers from Evrart Claire for a youth centre in the Fishing Village; it needs signatures from two residents.",
      "details": "Inside are the construction documents: a building period of 12 to 40 months and a zoning plan for a three-storey youth centre jutting into the sea and covering most of the village's street and square. Evrart wants it signed by Isobel Sadie (the Washerwoman) and Lilienne Carter, the net picker, and then mailed back to him.",
      "spoiler": "Both women are wary of Union paperwork. You can also try forging the signatures or getting the village drunks to sign, but Logic points out that the drunks' signatures are worthless.",
      "seeAlso": [
        "evrart-claire",
